<a href="https://www.techradar.com/home/smart-home/a-really-fun-hard-fought-journey-i-spoke-with-apple-about-the-engineering-behind-homeview-and-why-it-took-so-long"><em>TechRadar</em>'s Jacob Krol interviewed</a> Apple's Vice President of Hardware Engineering Matthew Costello about Apple's all-new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/12/apple-homeview-review/">HomeView</a> smart home display, which is available starting today. The discussion was largely focused on the HomeView's design, with Costello touching on the device achieving a display-related record for Apple products.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/homeview-lifestyle.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070346" /><br/>
Specifically, the HomeView's display brightness <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/13/homeview-can-dim-to-lowest-ever-brightness/">can automatically go down to just 0.3 nits</a>, which is a record low for any Apple product. This ultra-low brightness makes the HomeView especially ideal for a bedside table at night. <br/>
<br/>
"I really love the fact that this is the lowest light performance we've ever engineered into a product, so it's down to 0.3 nits," said Costello.<br/>
<br/>
"So officially, I represent the most dim product ever inside of Apple," he quipped.<br/>
<br/>
For comparison, some other Apple products like the latest iPhones and iPad mini are advertised as having a minimum 1-nit display brightness.<br/>
<br/>
HomeView's maximum display brightness is 500 nits.<br/>
<br/>
Unsurprisingly, Costello said the HomeView is designed for the home (truly shocking) and Siri AI.<br/>
<br/>
"It really was constructed around Siri," he said. <br/>
<br/>
"We really custom-built this user interface for the home, so the apps and experiences that matter most in the home setting are really front and center," he added.<br/>
<br/>
"There's no logging in, logging out, which is super cool. It recognizes you and your information, and when you step away, it's gone."<br/>
